> planner/types.py
> """
> Shared immutable-ish domain types for planning, selection, execution,
> feedback, provenance, and durable state.
> 
> Important design rules:
> - A response is attributed to a concrete selected PlanSpec/version, never to
>   mutable state such as `selector.last_responder`.
> - Canonical user/assistant transcript messages are append-only and auditable.
> - Internal context, tool outputs, and async results belong in typed artifacts
>   and explicit state, not silently rewritten transcript text.
> - Tool configuration is part of plan identity and therefore learnable.
> - Full raw tool results may be retained temporarily; durable source material
>   should preserve exact excerpts actually relevant to a response.
> """
> 
