> }
> ```
> 
> `execute_llm_text()` must:
> 
> 1. Read inherited execution budget from `invocation.provenance_requirements`.
> 2. Reject depth beyond `max_recursion_depth`.
> 3. Select an explicitly requested model, or call ordinary `Planner._select_plan()`.
> 4. Persist a child `ExecutionRun(parent_run_id=parent_run_id, depth=parent.depth + 1)`.
> 5. Parse output with `extract_plan()`.
> 6. Execute a child plan only if present.
> 7. Return only bounded JSON-safe data.
> 
> ### Test
> 
> ```python
> def test_llm_text_plan_creates_child_run(runtime, registered_llm_tool):
>     result = runtime.execute(parent_plan, {}, execution=parent_context)
>     assert result["child_run_id"]
>     child = repo.get_execution_run(result["child_run_id"])
>     assert child.parent_run_id == parent_context.run_id
>     assert child.depth == 1
> ```
