> 
> ## 7. Security gate before production use
> 
> Do not rely on the current regex validator as a sandbox boundary. At minimum:
> 
> - run Deno with `--deny-all`;
> - add OS process CPU/memory/file-descriptor limits;
> - kill the entire process group on timeout;
> - bound stdout/stderr bytes;
> - reject recursion and unbounded `for`/`for...of` until AST validation exists;
> - replace regex validation with Tree-sitter parsing before allowing arbitrary model-authored plans.
> 
> The current `AsyncFunction` approach is acceptable only when Deno is genuinely permissionless and externally resource-limited.
